        "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice ([[def-axiom-of-choice]]) as in\n[[prop-qft-four-dimensional-log-scale-anomaly]]. That proposition gives an\nexact Euclidean distribution-extension identity for the specified punctured\nkernel $u(x)=1/(16\\pi^4|x|^4)$: changing its cutoff scale changes the\nextension by $(8\\pi^2)^{-1}\\log(\\mu/\\nu)\\delta_0$. Its statement\nexplicitly says this is not a measured running coupling or physical beta\nfunction. The identity does not select a physical renormalization\nprescription, define an experimental observable, or construct a\nLorentzian interacting field. This remark asserts neither existence nor\nnonexistence of a continuum interacting model and supplies no empirical\nclaim.",
